==Strategy==
Use [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] to kill the first Gobble, then spam [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Future Cats]] and use [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]] to hold Oldhorn in place. After that, use him as a stepping stone for more Jellycats and other [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|wave units]]. Enough DPS will keep the Gobbles from interfering. Once they are all dead, kill Oldhorn and win. [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] is great at this, with his [[Massive Damage]] to Relics.

Alternatively, if Headmaster Cat Jobs is unavailable, you can make use of [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Doctor Cat]]'s [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] [[Talents|Talent]]. Do a similar start off to before, luring the initial Gobble out and using Fishman Cat and Jellycat to kill him. After that Gobble is dead, start stacking Doctor Cats and [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance attackers]] such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Medalist Cat]], [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]], or any suitable Long Distance [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]]. Research [[Cat Combo|Combos]] are recommended to allow a bigger stack more quickly. The large stack of Doctor Cats should repeatedly push Oldhorn and interrupt Gobble's attack animation while the Long Distance stack kills them off. If the [[Enemy Bases|enemy base]] is reached and the double Gobble wave destroys your stack, they can be lured to base and then destroyed like the first one using [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. Doctor Cat will save Oldhorn from destroying your base and then you've won.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Generally, almost any Long Distance Uber should do well here, as long as they have enough effective range to snipe Gobble from behind Oldhorn. Any Uber a special ability against Relic and/or [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies should also do well here. Below are more specified examples of good Ubers to use in this stage
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: Can deal insanely high single target damage to the Oldhorn, so long as you're able to keep him stalled and keep the Gobbles in check.
*[[The 6th Angel (Uber Rare Cat)|The 6th Angel]]: although a collab unit, the 6th angel has the longest forward piercing range in the game, along with massive damage VS floating and surge. This makes her an ideal unit to use on this stage should you have her.
*[[Megurine Luka (Uber Rare Cat)|Megurine Luka]]: Deals massive damage to the Gobbles in this stage, just be wary of her two knockbacks.
*[[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Empress Chronos]]: [[Freeze|Freezes]] Oldhorn to a halt while also hitting Gobble. With her, you'll barely have to wary about Oldhorn advancing at all.
*[[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Radiant Aphrodite]]: Aphrodite is able to keep the Gobbles at bay, and can reposition well during this stage due to her four knockbacks.
*[[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]]: Uses Oldhorn as a stepping stone in order to do massive damage to the Gobbles from behind, just don't let Gobble attack or Oldhorn advance too far.
*[[CAT-10 Gigapult]]: with immune to toxic and effective against relic. This stage becomes trivial with meatshielding

==Trivia==
*This was the first stage to have a buffed [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemy on 1-Crown difficulty, that being a 200% [[Oldhorn]].
*While other stages in Nasi-Go-Round directly reference specific areas of Southeast Asia, this stage instead brings up its dishes, specifically chicken fried rice and its variations: delicacies found commonly throughout all of Southeast Asia.
**The gobbles presumably represent the meat choice of the dish in this specific instance.

